          "date": "2026-11-16 23:05:43.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-18938 target: do not wait for object frees on lock cancel",
        "message": "LU-18938 target: do not wait for object frees on lock cancel\n\nA cross-MDT lock cancel syncs the whole target so that the\nother MDT sees the updates under the lock committed. Since\nthe delayed object free, that sync also waits for a pass of\nthe free work over every target on the node. After a large\nunlink that pass can take minutes, and the cancel needs only\nthe commit.\n\nWait for the frees only on an OST_SYNC of the whole target,\nas before.\n\nFixes: 444d29c21891 (\"LU-18938 obdclass: delay an object free\")\nTest-Parameters: mdscount=2 mdtcount=4 testlist=sanityn,sanity-quota\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I28a77bd4f2cc91ec9051d5fa3d2873a2cf876f4e\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
